  "body": "The maintainer asked for this on 2026-11-14, during the v0.20.0 cut: \"we need to break up that heavy lane into multiple smaller tests so we can pinpoint an exact test instead of having to run everything everytime for every little fix.\"\n\nWhat happens now:\n- `cargo xtask gate release` runs each heavy lane as one step, for example `app heavy lane (release --ignored)`.\n- One step runs every `#[ignore]`d test of the crate. The v0.20.0 gate took 86.6 minutes.\n- One failed test (`shared_face_bodies`, issue 1706) made the full step red. The log does not show a result for each binary at the step level.\n- To check a small fix, a session must run the full lane again or write the `cargo test` command by hand.\n\nWhat we want:\n- The release tier plans one step for each heavy test binary (`app heavy: shared_face_bodies`, `app heavy: pocket3d_hsm`, and so on) for the app, motion and kernel heavy lanes.\n- Each step has its own log file and its own pass or fail line with its wall time.\n- The gate summary names each failed binary and each failed test.\n- A session can run one heavy binary, or one heavy test, by name through `cargo xtask gate`.\n- The release build is made one time. The steps then run the built binaries.\n- A heavy test that takes more than a stated limit is reported by name with its time.\n\nRelated work:\n- Issue 1702 (PR 1704) adds `--only <step>` and `--failed <gate-logs dir>`. With one step for each binary, these options select an exact binary.\n- Issue 1703 covers parallel lanes. Small steps are the units that the parallel lanes run.\n\nDone means:\n- `cargo xtask gate release --dry-run` lists one step for each heavy test binary.\n- A failed heavy test makes only the step of its binary red, and the summary names the test.\n- `cargo xtask gate release --only \"<step of one binary>\"` runs that binary only.\n- The `#[test]` count of the heavy lanes is the same before and after the change.\n- The xtask unit tests pin the plan.\n- AGENTS.md \"Three gate tiers\" describes the steps. The PR body carries `Process change: yes`.\n",
